      "side": 1,
      "message": "Tests were the reason I first added this (before realizing that we can\u0027t yet `unwrap` in `const` context) but I agree that pvmfw is unlikely to have hardcoded phandles. Anyway, there\u0027s no harm in having a `const` constructor.\n\n\u003e I\u0027m worrying whether having `Phandle::new()` encourages bad pattern or not.\n\nI get where you\u0027re coming from (although note that we already have `::new()` in the code) but should we really prevent something at the Rust level because it _most of the time_ (not always!) is bad practice in DTS? There are good reasons for wanting to access `phandles` by values known at compile time.",
